# Items eqy_rtl (gate mode) and eqy_rtl_00 / eqy_rtl_11 (RTL mode): the design under test
# against the golden RTL (snapshot/divider.v) at the same configuration (LATCH_DENOMINATOR,
# CHECK_INVALID). Gate mode: the netlist's Yosys view divider_fv.v (netlist + combinational
# PDK models + liberty flop models). RTL mode: the candidate RTL with the same chparam lines.
# run_all.sh replaces @LD@ / @CI@ with the configuration and @GATEPARAM@ with the chparam
# lines (RTL mode) or nothing (gate mode). Strategy sat, depth 1: the state bits are matched
# by name and each partition's next-state and output functions are proven equal, an
# unbounded equivalence proof. This is the mandatory candidate-vs-golden equivalence (D9b).
# Matching: ports and registers by name. The golden's combinational wire names are excluded
# ([match], gold-nomatch): a netlist may keep such a name on a net that ABC optimised under a
# don't-care (seen: next_quotient[0] differs in IDLE, where it is unused), which is not an
# inequivalence. All partitions are merged into one ([partition], merge *): separate
# partitions would treat a matched output that is a function of matched state (busy, a
# function of state) as an independent free input, which gives spurious "unknown" results.
# dffunmap on both sides: enable / reset flops become plain flops with explicit feedback.
# It is a STRICT equivalence: it does not use the 0/0 caller guarantees (SPEC A1-A4), so a
# candidate that exploits them fails here and needs a reviewed, domain-restricted proof. A
# netlist that re-encodes the state (no name match) gives "equivalence unknown" (failed).
[gold]
read_verilog -sv gold.v
chparam -set LATCH_DENOMINATOR 1 divider
chparam -set CHECK_INVALID 1 divider
hierarchy -top divider
proc
prep -top divider
dffunmap

[gate]
read_verilog -sv gate.v

hierarchy -top divider
proc; flatten; opt_clean
prep -top divider
dffunmap

[match *]
# at 11 the mapped netlist names the saved_divisor / invalid_r flops after the golden's
# combinational aliases (divisor = saved_divisor, invalid = invalid_r at CHECK_INVALID = 1)
gold-match g_divisor.saved_divisor divisor
gold-match invalid_r invalid
gold-nomatch magnitude
gold-nomatch trial
gold-nomatch difference
gold-nomatch subtract
gold-nomatch next_remainder
gold-nomatch next_quotient
gold-nomatch rounded
gold-nomatch signed_result
gold-nomatch overflow
gold-nomatch invalid
gold-nomatch divisor

[partition *]
merge *

[strategy sat]
use sat
depth 1
